  "description": "Cheon Woo-Jeong, who was looking for a high-paying short-term part-time job. While working as a cruise staff member, he met a passenger… \n\n“Do you also interpret?”\n\n“English and… a little Filipino.” \n\n“Would you mind using your mouth for me and taking my money, Cheon Woo-Jeong?” \n\nThe man suggested. I needed money, and he said he needed my mouth. So the whole fault was mine for interpreting his words so literally.\n\n *“Just shut your upper mouth and open your lower mouth.” \n\n“…Huh?”\n\n“This is fun. Did you think I could do something great?”\n\n“I think there’s some misunderstanding. You clearly said you needed an interpreter back then…” \n\n“When did I?”\n\n“You said that…”\n\n“This is no fun, Cheon Woo-Jeong. It’s not enough to crawl on all fours and beg you to be nice to me.”*\n\nWhen I came to my senses, the ship was already drifting in an unexpected direction.\n\n(Source: Ridibooks, translated)",
